                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Oculus Touch Gameplay: https://youtu.be/UXSzc3BE1U0\n\nRollerCoaster Legends is a VR roller-coaster experience, with a Greek mythology theme. Gameplay involves riding a rollercoaster through the Temple of Poseidon, the River Styx, Tartarus, and the Palace of Hades. You also encounter icons from Greek mythology including the Minotaur, Kronos, Charon, and Hades whilst in these environments. The environments are very immersive, but I do think the sound effects of the track/cart could be improved slightly, and I would have liked the track to be a continuous feature of the game, to make the experience even more immersive. The environments are immersive though and simultaneously visually stunning. I found the experience enjoyable and unique, and therefore recommend this game. Gameplay is short, lasting around ten minutes, but the experience is fun and unlike any other VR roller-coaster I have yet to experience. (Also, I was happy to find that I did not experience any motion-sickness.)",
